			(it costs at most one doc of Z - but the slope term collapses to)
			(nearly zero on a near-vertical wall and then rejects a perfectly)
			(good extension: the end wall of testing_15_2 needs 0.5080 and was)
			(cut off, leaving every level 0.508 short of the pre-finish wall)
			(and one pass behind the boss plunging. 3 x doc covers segments)
			(down to about 18 degrees on its own; the slope term takes over)
			(below that. Largest legitimate extension measured on two projects)
			(is 1.0034, the bogus one 19.4436, so the two are nowhere near)
			(this bound.)
			#<s_reach> = [3.0 * #<_rough_cut>]
			o<s_rch> if [ABS[#<s_cx> - #<s_px>] GT 0.000001]
				#<s_slp> = [1.5 * #<_rough_cut> * ABS[#<s_cz> - #<s_pz>] / ABS[#<s_cx> - #<s_px>]]
				o<s_rch2> if [#<s_slp> GT #<s_reach>]
					#<s_reach> = #<s_slp>
				o<s_rch2> endif
			o<s_rch> endif
			(A CROSSING BEYOND THE REACH IS CLAMPED, NOT REJECTED. Rejecting it)
			(stops the level on the floor allowance, and over a chamfer that)
			(leaves a 0.447 mm stub where the feature is 1 mm long. greatEndian)
			(chose to let the pass run past the floor stop and cut nearer the)
			(contour than fin_off + prefin_off allows, so the reach becomes the)
			(LENGTH of the extension rather than a test on it. Levels whose)
			(crossing already lies inside the reach - every one on both test)
			(projects, 0.90 to 1.0034 mm - are untouched.)
