					#<s_zc> = #<s_fz>
				o<s_cl2> else
					#<s_zc> = [#<z_end> - [#<z_dir> * #<s_reach>]]
				o<s_cl2> endif
			o<s_clamp> endif
			o<s_fwd> if [[[#<z_dir> * [#<s_zc> - #<z_end>]] LT -0.0001] AND [[#<z_dir> * [#<s_zc> - #<w_to>]] GT -0.0001]]
					(A CLAMPED CANDIDATE MUST NOT BEAT A REAL CROSSING. The)
					(clamp is the answer to "no crossing within reach" - it)
					(runs the level to the end of the feature - and it lands)
					(NEARER THE FRONT than a genuine crossing does, so the)
					(nearest-wins rule below handed it the pass.)
					(Measured on testing_15_5: the level at r32.7000 crosses)
					(the pre-finish contour three times - the boss front face)
					(at Z-29.4588, its back face at Z-36.4467 and the end of)
					(the part at Z-69.8920. The two far ones are out of reach)
					(and clamp back to the feature boundary at Z-28.3891,)
					(which is in front of the real crossing, so the pass)
					(stopped 1.0697 mm short of the contour it should have)
					(ended on. greatEndian: the 3rd, 4th and 5th passes are)
					(not tangent to the pre-finish contour.)
					(An unclamped candidate wins outright; among equals the)
					(nearest to the front still wins, exactly as before.)
					#<s_take> = 0
					o<s_near> if [#<s_have> EQ 0]
						#<s_take> = 1
					o<s_near> elseif [[#<s_bcl> GT 0] AND [#<s_cl> EQ 0]]
						#<s_take> = 1
					o<s_near> elseif [[#<s_bcl> EQ #<s_cl>] AND [[#<z_dir> * [#<s_zc> - #<s_best>]] GT 0]]
						#<s_take> = 1
					o<s_near> endif
					o<s_set> if [#<s_take>]
						#<s_best> = #<s_zc>
						#<s_bcl>  = #<s_cl>
						#<s_have> = 1
					o<s_set> endif
				o<s_fwd> endif
			o<s_cross> endif
			#<s_pz> = #<s_cz>
			#<s_px> = #<s_cx>
		o<s_w> endwhile
		(A CLAMPED CANDIDATE MUST NOT EXTEND THE CUT. A clamp is a guess at)
		(reach - z_end plus or minus s_reach - not a measured crossing, so it)
		(may pull a cut IN to a feature the scan could not see, but it may)
		(never push one PAST where the scan already stopped.)
		(Measured on testing_15_2 with the axial allowance at 2.000, once the)
		(stop contour carries the pre-finish allowance and so coincides with)
		(the floor: the scan correctly ended at Z-68.146, 2.254 from the wall,)
		(and a clamped candidate with no real crossing behind it - bcl=1 -)
		(dragged it to Z-69.670, exactly z_end minus the 1.524 reach, cutting)
		(to 0.730 from a wall told to keep 2.254.)
		o<s_ok> if [#<s_have>]
			o<s_push> if [[#<s_bcl> GT 0] AND [[#<z_dir> * [#<s_best> - #<z_end_scan>]] LT 0]]
				(clamped, and it would cut further than the scan - ignore it)
			o<s_push> else
				#<z_end> = #<s_best>
			o<s_push> endif
		o<s_ok> endif
	o<stp> endif


	(THE PROFILE-ANGLE APPROACH IS ARMED HERE, AFTER THE STOP, not up in the)
	(entry block where its inputs are found. Its cap - never longer than the)
	(cut it is entering - was being tested against the SCAN's z_end, and the)
	(stop table then extends that cut. On testing_15_2 the last pass behind the)
	(boss came out 2.6397 long against a 2.2004 ramp, so the ramp fitted, but)
	(the pre-extension length did not clear it: that pass alone lost its ramp)
	(and plunged in at 45 degrees instead of arriving along the surface. It is)
	(visible as the odd one out because Sectioning gives that region a longer)
	(window and the same cap then passes - greatEndian: "if I select sectioning)
	(the lead in shape is right".)
	(the crossing that set the START if there was one, else the nearest)
	(crossing there is - the angle to arrive at does not depend on whether)
	(the pass was allowed to start early)
	(THE TABLE FIRST, and the crossings only when there is no table.)
	(A crossing names the segment the level happens to meet, which is not)
	(always the surface the pass will run along: behind the boss on)
	(testing_15_5 the level at r33.1273 crosses the near-FLAT top of the)
	(boss, slope 0.0566, and copying that gave a ramp 8.9734 long where)
	(every neighbour runs 2.2004. Python already answers this properly for)
	(every segment - the dominant surface just ahead of it - so ask it)
	(rather than the crossing. The crossing branches stay for a program)
	(generated before the table existed.)
	o<e_pick> if [#<e_whave>]
		#<e_rdz> = #<e_wdz>
		#<e_rdx> = #<e_wdx>
	o<e_pick> elseif [#<e_have>]
		#<e_rdz> = #<e_bdz>
		#<e_rdx> = #<e_bdx>
	o<e_pick> elseif [#<e_ahave>]
		#<e_rdz> = #<e_adz>
		#<e_rdx> = #<e_adx>
	o<e_pick> endif
	o<e_arm> if [[ABS[#<e_rdz>] GT 0.000001] AND [#<_rough_cut> GT 0]]
		#<e_slope> = [#<e_rdx> / #<e_rdz>]
		#<e_asl>   = ABS[#<e_slope>]
		(the depth of cut is a RADIAL quantity, so it is PROJECTED onto the)
		(contour's own angle rather than used as a length: one depth of cut of)
		(radius costs doc/sin of the angle along the segment and doc/tan of it)
		(in Z. On a 13 degree ramp that is 2.20 mm of Z for a 0.508 mm cut.)
		o<e_proj> if [#<e_asl> GT 0.000001]
			#<pa_dz> = [#<_rough_cut> / #<e_asl>]
			(NEVER LONGER THAN THE CUT IT IS ENTERING - now the REAL one.)
			(SHORTENED to fit rather than dropped: a ramp that does not fit)
			(used to be abandoned altogether and the pass then plunged in at)
			(45 degrees, which is the shape greatEndian reported behind the)
			(boss. How long the approach is was never the point - arriving)
			(PARALLEL to the surface it is about to leave is - and a short)
			(ramp at the contour's own angle does that just as well as a full)
			(one. Whether the full ramp fits depends on where the ladder's)
			(levels happen to fall against the slope, so any change to the)
			(levels can turn a ramped pass into a plunging one; giving the)
			(short pass the ramp it can have removes that coupling.)
			(THE LENGTH IS NOT A FREE CHOICE THOUGH - it is what makes the)
			(ramps CHAIN. Every ramp runs doc/sin of the contour angle, and the)
			(levels sit one doc apart, so consecutive ramps are parallel lines)
			(whose end is exactly the next one's start. Capping one breaks that)
			(chain and it shows as a lead-in hanging in space, half the length)
			(of its neighbours. greatEndian, 2026-08-31: *"parallel artificial)
			(lead ins are every second time halfsized ... artificial lead in)
			(should start at endings of lead in from segment before"*.)
			(Measured on testing_15_9: the standard ramp is 2.1724 and the last)
			(of each section came out 1.0544, 0.9436, 0.8671, 0.7905, 0.7139 -)
			(each exactly half its own cut, which is what the cap here was.)
			(The cap was there so a ramp could not eat its whole pass. It does)
			(not need to: the ramp runs through metal that is ALREADY GONE -)
