				(THE RAMP MUST COME IN FROM THE STOCK SIDE. Its whole job is)
				(to arrive parallel to the surface through material that is)
				(already gone; a direction that puts its start INSIDE the)
				(level dives into the part and climbs back out, which is)
				(what greatEndian saw at the front of testing_15_5 - the)
				(lead-in descending to r33.7160, the NEXT pass's level, then)
				(returning to r34.2240 at Z0. The entry segment there rises)
				(with the front face, so copying its angle points the wrong)
				(way. No ramp is the right answer in that case, and the)
