	(the same profile-angle ramp, the same cut - emitted end to start instead)
	(of start to end. That is what makes it remove exactly the same metal,)
	(and it is greatEndian's spec read literally: same G-code, movement from)
	(the last polyline reference to the front.)
	(So there is no reversed frame here any more. Each lead belongs to an END)
	(of the pass and keeps its own geometry in both directions - the li lead)
	(at the z_start end, the lo lead at the z_end end - and the only thing)
	(_pl_cut_rev decides is which of the two is traversed INWARD as the)
	(approach and which outward as the retreat. e_dir is gone with it: it was)
	(a second frame, and a second frame is what analysis/054 removed from the)
	(decomposition for exactly the same reason.)

	(resolve the lead-out radius and the possibly-shortened cut end BEFORE the)
	(straight cut, so a cut ending near a wall can stop just early enough that)
	(a full-radius lead-out arc still lands tangent to the pre-finish contour)
	(instead of the radius being clipped to a constant. z_end - the logical)
	(floor crossing - is left untouched for the interval/blocking logic and)
	(the _pl_level_z_end export; only the physical straight-cut endpoint and)
	(the fillet's own tangent point move)
	#<z_end_cut> = #<z_end>

	o<lo_res> if [[#<lo_len> GT 0] OR [#<lo_rad> GT 0]]
		(lead-out line direction: unit vector pointing from the exit toward)
		(the far rapid point - 0 degrees along Z surface, 90 radial)
		#<lo_bz> = [#<z_dir> * COS[#<lo_ang>]]
		#<lo_bx> = [#<_pl_x_sgn> * SIN[#<lo_ang>]]
		#<_lo_cos> = [#<z_dir> * #<lo_bz>]
		#<_lo_leff> = #<lo_len>

		(mirrors the lead-in's own _li_leff/li_cap_all cap above, and bounds the)
		(same end of the interval it does. The retreat travels BACKWARD, from)
		(z_end toward w_from, for either z_dir - lo_bz carries z_dir, so the)
		(move Z[end_z + _lo_leff * lo_bz] always runs against the cutting)
		(direction. What it must not reach past is therefore w_from: on a)
		(multi-crossing continuation interval that is where the boss blocking)
		(the sweep sits. Measuring toward w_to instead bounded the one direction)
		(the retreat never travels, which both deleted the lead-out outright)
		(whenever a pass ran its whole window - z_end clamped to w_to, so zero)
		(room, which is what left every artificial slice ending bare - and let)
		(a continuation interval retreat run back over its own start when the)
		(room ahead happened to be large. Gated on multi-crossing so the)
		(single-crossing path stays byte-for-byte unchanged)
		(NOT ON THE FIRST INTERVAL. This cap keeps a continuation interval's)
		(retreat from running back over its own start, where the boss that)
		(blocked the sweep is sitting. The first interval has no such)
		(obstruction behind it - it starts at the polyline's Begin Z and)
		(everything in front of that is air - so capping there just takes)
		(the lead the operator asked for: on testing_15_4's chamfer level a)
		(1.000 mm lead came out 0.125 because the cut is 0.088 long.)
		(Not gated on the emission direction: this cap belongs to the lo lead)
		(at the z_end END of the pass, and that lead sits at the same place)
		(with the same length whichever way the cut is emitted. Only whether)
		(it is travelled outward or inward changes.)
		o<lo_cap_all> if [[#<_pl_multi_cross> GT 0] AND [#<w_from> LT [#<_pl_begin_z> - 0.000001]]]
			#<_lo_room> = ABS[#<z_end> - #<w_from>]
			o<lo_lcap> if [#<_lo_cos> GT 0.0001]
