	(previously PROCESSED window cut - and that is only the neighbour the lead)
	(enters when the processing order follows the part. It does under)
	(Artificial front-to-back and back-to-front, and it does NOT under Natural,)
	(which orders windows weakest/smallest-diameter first, nor under Both)
	(directions, which alternates the entry END per pass so every other pass)
	(leads in over the boundary with a section not yet cut.)
	(Measured with the carried value left live in those two: Natural rapided)
	(0.4962 to 0.4991 mm and Both directions 0.5059 mm INTO STANDING METAL -)
	(one full depth of cut - where both are clean before. They were bounded)
	(out, and greatEndian, 2026-08-31: *"do same for natural sectionning and)
	(both directions"*.)
	(So the question is asked of the WINDOWS THE LEAD ACTUALLY CROSSES.)
	(#2800 + i holds the deepest level window i has cut so far, written below)
	(and cleared to 999999 by lathe_sections. Take the MAXIMUM over every)
	(window the lead's Z span touches except this one: the lead is air only if)
