					#<ld_seen> = 1
					#<ld_d> = #[2800 + #<ld_i>]
					o<ld_mx> if [#<ld_d> GT #<ld_ref>]
						#<ld_ref> = #<ld_d>
					o<ld_mx> endif
				o<ld_take> endif
			o<ld_self> endif
			#<ld_i> = [#<ld_i> + 1]
		o<ld_w> endwhile
		(no window touched means the lead reaches into ground nothing here)
		(describes - the front of the part, outside the sectioned span - so)
		(there is no evidence it is cleared and the lead stays.)
		(debug LDG w=%d lvl=%f seen=%d ref=%f z0=%f z1=%f)
		o<ld_deep> if [[#<ld_seen> GT 0] AND [#<level> GE [#<ld_ref> - 0.000001]]]
			#<ld_air> = 1
			(the ramp goes with it. Disarming ONLY the ramp is what made an)
			(earlier attempt at this worth 22% instead of the measured 35%:)
			(the pass did not lose its approach, it fell back to the plain)
			(1.0 mm lead at 45 degrees - an X step of 0.7072, DEEPER than one)
			(depth of cut - so the air time came back as a plunge. The lead)
			(lengths are zeroed with it below, which drops the pass onto the)
			(no-lead path that already exists and is already proven: stand)
			(off in Z by the clearance, descend X there through the cleared)
			(column, cut. Nothing new is invented for this.)
			#<pa_on> = 0
		o<ld_deep> endif
	o<ld_gate> endif

	(THE STRAIGHT LEAD AT THE z_start END, resolved here beside the other one)
	(rather than inside the block that emits it, because which of the two is)
	(emitted first depends on the direction and both have to be in hand by)
	(then. Pure arithmetic - it emits nothing, so front to back is unchanged.)
	#<li_bz> = [#<z_dir> * COS[#<li_ang>]]
	#<li_bx> = [#<_pl_x_sgn> * SIN[#<li_ang>]]
	#<_li_leff> = #<li_len>
	#<_li_reff> = #<li_rad>
	(multi-crossing continuation intervals can be short - the lead's own)
	(depth excursion, li_len times cos of li_ang, must not reach past z_end,)
	(or the lead line itself would cut into territory this interval was)
	(never meant to touch. z_end is already known here regardless of)
	(whether this is the first or a later interval, so cap against the)
	(actual room instead of the caller unconditionally zeroing the whole)
	(lead for every interval after the first. Gated on multi-crossing so)
	(the single-crossing path is byte-for-byte unchanged - it never had)
	(this cap and first intervals there are assumed to have enough room.)
	(li_rad itself is deliberately left uncapped, matching the contour)
	(pass's own lead-in in lathe_poly_pass.ngc, which has never capped)
	(it either - only the straight length risks cutting past z_end)
	(NOT ON THE FIRST INTERVAL. This cap keeps a continuation interval's)
	(approach from running back over its own start, where the boss that)
	(blocked the sweep is sitting. The first interval has no such)
	(obstruction behind it - it starts at the polyline's Begin Z and)
	(everything in front of that is air - so capping there just takes)
	(the lead the operator asked for: on testing_15_4's chamfer level a)
	(1.000 mm lead came out 0.125 because the cut is 0.088 long.)
	o<li_cap_all> if [[#<_pl_multi_cross> GT 0] AND [#<w_from> LT [#<_pl_begin_z> - 0.000001]]]
		#<_li_room> = ABS[#<z_end> - #<w_from>]
		#<_li_cos>  = [#<z_dir> * #<li_bz>]
		o<li_lcap> if [#<_li_cos> GT 0.0001]
			#<_li_lmax> = [#<_li_room> / #<_li_cos>]
			o<li_lcap2> if [#<_li_leff> GT #<_li_lmax>]
				#<_li_leff> = #<_li_lmax>
			o<li_lcap2> endif
		o<li_lcap> endif
	o<li_cap_all> endif

	(WHICH END THE TOOL ARRIVES AT. em_z0 is where the cut begins and em_z1)
	(where it ends, in emission order; with _pl_cut_rev 0 they are the pass's)
	(own start and its physical cut end, exactly as before.)
	#<em_z0> = #<z_start>
	#<em_z1> = #<z_end_cut>
	o<rev_em> if [#<_pl_cut_rev> GT 0]
		#<em_z0> = #<z_end_cut>
		#<em_z1> = #<z_start>
	o<rev_em> endif

	(Skip a pass too short to be worth making. A level whose cut is only a)
	(fraction of the tool sits almost entirely inside the pre-finish allowance)
	(anyway - the contour pass that follows takes the same metal in one go - so)
	(cutting it costs an approach and a retract to remove almost nothing.)
	(BEFORE the approach and the lead-in, not after them: returning later still)
	(left the whole entry behind - retract, rapid to the lead start, then a FEED)
	(into the workpiece - and then walked away without cutting the pass it had)
	(just entered for. A skipped pass now emits no motion at all.)
	(Measured on z_end_cut, which is why the lead-out resolution above it moved)
	(up here too: that block is pure arithmetic, it emits nothing, and the pull)
	(back it applies is what decides how long this cut really is. Measuring the)
	(raw crossing instead read the pass longer than it is and the gate missed)
	(the passes it exists for.)
	(_pl_level_z_end is already set above, so the disjoint-interval scan still)
	(knows where this level reached and carries on past it.)
	(measured on the pass's OWN two ends, not on the emission order - the cut)
	(is the same length whichever way round it is made)
	(A CUT THAT DOES NOT ADVANCE IS NOT A CUT, and this is not the same)
	(question as the length one below. The window travels from w_from to w_to,)
	(z_dir is 1 when that runs toward decreasing Z, and a real cut therefore)
	(always has z_dir * [z_start - z_end_cut] POSITIVE. Where the level has)
	(dropped below everything it could reach, the scan hands back a start from)
	(the entry contour and an end from the stop contour that have CROSSED, and)
	(the pass came out running backwards along its own window.)
	(Measured on testing_15_7, roughing back to front so every real cut runs)
	(toward increasing Z: a 0.3304 mm pass at X25.3728 from Z-69.5918 to)
	(Z-69.9222 - the wrong way - sitting under a ladder whose other levels run)
	(1.8609, 4.0522, 6.2435, 8.4348 the right way at a 0.5059 X step. Those)
	(lengths gain 2.1913 per level, so the next one down is -0.33: the level)
	(has NO material and the crossed interval is what got emitted instead of)
	(nothing. greatEndian, 2026-08-26: "this tiny pass is senseless it should)
	(not be there even with property off skipp short passes .. it has wrong)
	(location".)
	(SO IT IS UNCONDITIONAL, not gated on _pl_min_pass. Skip short is a saving)
	(the operator chooses and it measures ABS, which cannot see a sign; this)
	(is a geometric impossibility and has to go whether or not that is on.)
	(Returning here is already a supported path - _pl_level_z_end is set above,)
	(so the disjoint-interval scan still knows where this level reached.)
	o<inv> if [[#<z_dir> * [#<z_start> - #<z_end_cut>]] LE 0.000001]
		o<lathe_level_pass> return
	o<inv> endif

	o<shrt> if [#<_pl_min_pass> GT 0]
		o<shrt2> if [ABS[#<z_end_cut> - #<z_start>] LT #<_pl_min_pass>]
			o<lathe_level_pass> return
		o<shrt2> endif
	o<shrt> endif


	(approach: full retract above stock, or minimal retract just above the)
	(previous pass level - safe because that band is already cut)
	(MINIMAL RETRACT NEEDS A SAFE REFERENCE, NOT THE PREVIOUS LEVEL.)
	(_pl_prev_lvl alone means "the previous level", and it goes stale the)
	(moment a boss splits a level into disjoint intervals: the band above it)
	(is cut where the tool has been, but the boss between here and the next)
	(pass is still standing. That is why poly_lathe_mill forced full retract)
	(whenever multi-crossing was active, which is always - so the Minimal)
	(setting could never fire on any project.)
	(So the reference is the highest material BETWEEN WHERE THE TOOL IS AND)
	(WHERE IT IS GOING: the roughing floor's peak over that span, which is)
	(what will still be standing there, taken together with the previous)
	(level. The floor table is already emitted and the stop scan above walks)
	(it the same way. Read the table, move.)
	(Measured on testing_15_9, Full against Minimal, same 799 rapids either)
	(way: rapid distance 4688.3 -> 1898.3 mm, total roughing motion 6451.6)
	(-> 3661.6 mm. The tightest clearance any traverse keeps over the)
	(roughing floor is +1.0693 mm - the retract distance plus margin, never)
	(negative - which is the number that says this is safe and not merely)
	(shorter. greatEndian, 2026-08-31: "there is a lot of the cutting air)
	(passings".)
	(With no floor table there is nothing to verify against, so it falls back)
	(to the full retract rather than guessing - and so does ID work, whose)
	(retract is a different geometry this has not been measured against.)
	o<ret_md> if [[#<_pl_ret_mode> GT 0] AND [#<_pl_stop_n> GT 0] AND [#<_pl_side> EQ 0]]
		#<pk> = #<_pl_prev_lvl>
		#<k_lo> = #<pv_end_z>
		#<k_hi> = #<z_start>
		o<k_ord> if [#<k_lo> GT #<k_hi>]
			#<k_lo> = #<z_start>
			#<k_hi> = #<pv_end_z>
		o<k_ord> endif
		#<k_i> = 0
		#<k_pz> = #[#<_pl_stop_base>]
		#<k_px> = #[#<_pl_stop_base> + 1]
		o<k_w> while [#<k_i> LT [#<_pl_stop_n> - 1]]
			#<k_i> = [#<k_i> + 1]
			#<k_cz> = #[#<_pl_stop_base> + #<k_i> * 2]
			#<k_cx> = #[#<_pl_stop_base> + #<k_i> * 2 + 1]
			(any segment overlapping the traverse contributes its endpoints -)
			(a segment crossing the span is covered by them, since the floor)
			(is piecewise linear and a maximum sits at a breakpoint.)
			(BUILT IN FOUR SHORT TESTS, not one expression: the single)
			(condition this replaced was long enough for the interpreter to)
			(refuse the file outright with "Command too long", which is the)
			(line-length limit CLAUDE.md warns about.)
			#<k_ov1> = 0
			o<k_a> if [[#<k_pz> GE [#<k_lo> - 0.000001]] AND [#<k_pz> LE [#<k_hi> + 0.000001]]]
				#<k_ov1> = 1
			o<k_a> endif
			o<k_b> if [[#<k_cz> GE [#<k_lo> - 0.000001]] AND [#<k_cz> LE [#<k_hi> + 0.000001]]]
				#<k_ov1> = 1
			o<k_b> endif
			o<k_c> if [[[#<k_pz> - #<k_lo>] * [#<k_cz> - #<k_lo>]] LT 0]
				#<k_ov1> = 1
			o<k_c> endif
			o<k_d> if [[[#<k_pz> - #<k_hi>] * [#<k_cz> - #<k_hi>]] LT 0]
				#<k_ov1> = 1
			o<k_d> endif
			o<k_ov> if [#<k_ov1> GT 0]
				o<k_mp> if [#<k_px> GT #<pk>]
					#<pk> = #<k_px>
				o<k_mp> endif
				o<k_mc> if [#<k_cx> GT #<pk>]
					#<pk> = #<k_cx>
				o<k_mc> endif
			o<k_ov> endif
			#<k_pz> = #<k_cz>
			#<k_px> = #<k_cx>
		o<k_w> endwhile
		#<ret_x> = [[#<pk> + #<_pl_ret_dist>] * #<_diameter_mode>]
		o<ret_cap> if [#<ret_x> GT [#<_wp_dia_od> + #<_x_clear>]]
			#<ret_x> = [#<_wp_dia_od> + #<_x_clear>]
		o<ret_cap> endif
		o<hf_move> CALL [0] [#<ret_x>] [#<pass_feed>]
	o<ret_md> else
		o<rt_side> if [#<_pl_side> EQ 1]
			o<hf_move> CALL [0] [#<_pl_id_ret>] [#<pass_feed>]
		o<rt_side> else
			o<hf_move> CALL [0] [[#<_wp_dia_od> + #<_x_clear>]] [#<pass_feed>]
		o<rt_side> endif
	o<ret_md> endif
	(where the z_start END of the pass sits: the start of the profile-angle)
	(segment when there is one, else the pass start itself. The segment is NOT)
	(part of the lead - it is there whether or not a lead was asked for, and)
	(the project that wanted it has lead-in length and radius both 0.)
	#<ap_z> = #<z_start>
	#<ap_x> = #<level>
	o<ap_use> if [#<pa_on>]
		#<ap_z> = #<pa_z>
		#<ap_x> = #<pa_x>
	o<ap_use> endif

	(=== WHICH END IS ENTERED, AND WHICH IS LEFT ==========================)
	(A pass has a lead at each of its two ends and both are fixed geometry:)
	(the li lead at the z_start end and the lo lead at the z_end end, each on)
	(its own line, with its own blend circle, in BOTH directions. All that)
	(_pl_cut_rev decides is which of the two the tool drives IN along and)
	(which it leaves along - back to front is the front-to-back motion played)
	(backwards, so it sweeps the identical volume and removes the identical)
	(metal. That is why it needs no mirror table: there is nothing new to)
	(compute, only the same points visited last-first.)
	(ap_* is the lead the pass is ENTERED along, rt_* the one it LEAVES)
	(along. Front to back that is li then lo, which is what it always was;)
	(back to front it is lo then li.)
	(*_fz/_fx is the vector handed to fillet_lead, which is NOT the same as)
	(the direction the straight lead is travelled: the utility wants the lead)
	(line pointing away from the cut for a blend the path drives INTO, and)
	(the existing lead-out has always negated it for the same circle at the)
	(other end. Kept exactly as each end had it, so the two directions share)
	(one circle rather than computing two.)
	#<ap_bz> = #<ap_z>
	#<ap_bx> = #<ap_x>
	#<ap_vz> = #<li_bz>
	#<ap_vx> = #<li_bx>
	#<ap_fz> = #<li_bz>
	#<ap_fx> = #<li_bx>
	#<ap_ll> = #<_li_leff>
	#<ap_rr> = #<_li_reff>
	#<ap_ff> = #<li_feed>
	#<rt_bz> = #<z_end_cut>
	#<rt_bx> = #<level>
	#<rt_vz> = #<lo_bz>
	#<rt_vx> = #<lo_bx>
	#<rt_fz> = [0 - #<lo_bz>]
	#<rt_fx> = [0 - #<lo_bx>]
	#<rt_ll> = #<_lo_leff>
	#<rt_rr> = #<_lo_reff>
	#<rt_ff> = #<lo_feed>
	o<end_sw> if [#<_pl_cut_rev> GT 0]
		#<ap_bz> = #<z_end_cut>
		#<ap_bx> = #<level>
		#<ap_vz> = #<lo_bz>
		#<ap_vx> = #<lo_bx>
		#<ap_fz> = [0 - #<lo_bz>]
		#<ap_fx> = [0 - #<lo_bx>]
		#<ap_ll> = #<_lo_leff>
		#<ap_rr> = #<_lo_reff>
		#<ap_ff> = #<lo_feed>
		#<rt_bz> = #<ap_z>
		#<rt_bx> = #<ap_x>
		#<rt_vz> = #<li_bz>
		#<rt_vx> = #<li_bx>
		#<rt_fz> = #<li_bz>
		#<rt_fx> = #<li_bx>
		#<rt_ll> = #<_li_leff>
		#<rt_rr> = #<_li_reff>
		#<rt_ff> = #<li_feed>
	o<end_sw> endif

	(ld_air drops the ENTRY lead only. The retreat lead at the other end is)
	(left exactly as it was: it leaves the cut this pass has just made, which)
	(is metal that was standing a moment ago, so it is not the same question)
	(and it is not what was reported.)
	o<ld_zero> if [#<ld_air> GT 0]
		#<ap_ll> = 0
		#<ap_rr> = 0
	o<ld_zero> endif

	(drive in along the entry lead: rapid to its far point, feed down the)
	(straight, then blend onto the pass's own direction)
	o<lead_ap> if [[#<ap_ll> GT 0] OR [#<ap_rr> GT 0]]
		(a level pass always travels along Z at constant X, so the toolpath's)
		(own direction at the entry is always pure Z - no profile lookup needed)
		#<_flt_ok> = 0
		o<ap_geom> if [#<ap_rr> GT 0]
			o<fillet_lead> CALL [#<ap_bz>] [#<ap_bx>] [-#<z_dir>] [0] [#<ap_fz>] [#<ap_fx>] [#<ap_rr>] [#<z_dir>]
		o<ap_geom> endif

		o<li_base> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			#<li_baz> = #<_flt_t1z>
			#<li_bax> = #<_flt_t1x>
		o<li_base> else
			#<li_baz> = #<ap_bz>
			#<li_bax> = #<ap_bx>
		o<li_base> endif

		o<hf_move> CALL [1] [[#<li_baz> + #<ap_ll> * #<ap_vz>]] [#<pass_feed>]
		o<hf_move> CALL [0] [[[#<li_bax> + #<ap_ll> * #<ap_vx>] * #<_diameter_mode>]] [#<pass_feed>]
		(the lead feed applies to the STRAIGHT lead only - the blend radius is)
		(already cutting into the part at the pass's own direction, so it runs)
		(at the pass feed like the rest of the cut. With no lead feed set both)
		(resolve to the pass feed and the whole approach is one feed)
		F#<ap_ff>
		o<li_str> if [#<ap_ll> GT 0]
			G1 X[#<li_bax> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<li_baz>
		o<li_str> endif
		o<li_fsw> if [#<ap_ff> NE #<pass_feed>]
			F#<pass_feed>
		o<li_fsw> endif
		o<li_arc> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			(tangent blend from the lead line into the pass's own direction,)
			(instead of a sharp corner)
			o<li_arc_d> if [#<_flt_cw>]
				G2 X[#<ap_bx> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<ap_bz> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<li_bax>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<li_baz>]
			o<li_arc_d> else
				G3 X[#<ap_bx> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<ap_bz> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<li_bax>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<li_baz>]
			o<li_arc_d> endif
		o<li_arc> endif
		F#<pass_feed>
	o<lead_ap> else
		(Z APPROACH CLEARANCE ONLY WHERE THERE IS ROOM FOR IT. Front to)
		(back the pass starts in front of its cut, so standing off by the)
		(clearance and descending there descends through air. A reversed)
		(pass starts at the far end of its own interval, where the profile)
		(is rising - that is what stopped the cut - so the same stand-off)
		(would put the radial descent inside standing material. It descends)
		(at the interval end itself, where the floor allowance still leaves)
		(the surface lvl_d below this level.)
		#<ap_cz> = [#<ap_bz> + #<z_dir> * #<_pl_z_clear>]
		o<ap_rev> if [#<_pl_cut_rev> GT 0]
			#<ap_cz> = #<ap_bz>
		o<ap_rev> endif
		o<hf_move> CALL [1] [#<ap_cz>] [#<pass_feed>]
		o<hf_move> CALL [0] [[#<ap_bx> * #<_diameter_mode>]] [#<pass_feed>]
	o<lead_ap> endif

	(the profile-angle ramp, outside the lead branch on purpose. Front to)
	(back it is driven DOWN, from the ramp start onto the level at z_start,)
	(before the cut; back to front the pass arrives at z_start along the cut)
	(and climbs the same line afterwards - see pa_out below. Same two points,)
	(same wedge of metal, opposite order.)
	o<pa_cut> if [[#<pa_on>] AND [#<_pl_cut_rev> LE 0]]
		F#<pass_feed>
		G1 X[#<ap_x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<ap_z>
		(the turn onto the level, at the entry point)
		G1 X[#<level> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<z_start>
	o<pa_cut> endif


	(CHIP BREAKING. Without pecking this is one continuous cut, which is what)
	(it has always been and still is when _pl_peck_len is 0 - the else branch)
	(below is the original line, unchanged, so pecking off is a provable)
	(no-op.)
	(The peck points cannot be a Python table: the interval END is decided by)
	(the scan at runtime, so generation time does not know how long this cut)
	(is. What Python would compute is a repeating rule with no geometry in it)
	(- cut this far, back off that far - so the subroutine walks the rule and)
	(no shape is worked out here.)
	(THE RETRACT IS ALONG THE CUT, straight back the way the tool came, into)
	(the groove it has just made. That is the reference package's own wording)
	(and it is the safe direction: backing out radially would leave the)
	(compensated path and re-enter it, and re-entry is where gouges come from.)
	o<peck> if [[#<_pl_peck_len> GT 0.0001] AND [#<_pl_peck_ret> GT 0.0001]]
		#<pk_dir> = 1
		o<pk_sgn> if [#<em_z1> LT #<em_z0>]
			#<pk_dir> = -1
		o<pk_sgn> endif
		#<pk_left> = ABS[#<em_z1> - #<em_z0>]
		#<pk_at>   = #<em_z0>
		o<pk_w> while [#<pk_left> GT [#<_pl_peck_len> + 0.0001]]
			#<pk_at>   = [#<pk_at> + #<pk_dir> * #<_pl_peck_len>]
			#<pk_left> = [#<pk_left> - #<_pl_peck_len>]
			G1 Z#<pk_at>
			(back along the path, never past where this cut began)
			#<pk_bk> = [#<pk_at> - #<pk_dir> * #<_pl_peck_ret>]
			o<pk_clamp> if [[#<pk_dir> * [#<pk_bk> - #<em_z0>]] LT 0]
				#<pk_bk> = #<em_z0>
			o<pk_clamp> endif
			G1 Z#<pk_bk>
			(wait AT THE RETRACTED POINT, where the chip is already broken)
			(and free - a pause here lets it fall clear instead of being)
			(dragged back into the next cut. Nothing moves during it.)
			o<pk_dw> if [#<_pl_peck_dwell> GT 0.0001]
				G4 P#<_pl_peck_dwell>
			o<pk_dw> endif
			G1 Z#<pk_at>
		o<pk_w> endwhile
		G1 Z#<em_z1>
	o<peck> else
		G1 Z#<em_z1>
	o<peck> endif

	(THIS PASS CUT, so its level is the deepest THIS WINDOW has reached - the)
	(ladder descends, so the last write wins. Set after the cut on purpose: a)
	(pass that returned early above never reaches this line, and a level)
	(nobody cut must not be recorded as removed metal.)
	(Kept per window rather than as one running value, because the gate above)
	(asks its NEIGHBOURS what they have cleared and the windows do not run in)
	(Z order under Natural or Both directions. _pl_wdeep_ok is tested so a)
	(program generated before the table existed never writes into slots its)
	(own reader will not trust.)
	o<ld_rec> if [[#<_pl_sect_count> GT 0] AND [#<_pl_wdeep_ok> GT 0]]
		#[2800 + #<_pl_w_idx>] = #<level>
	o<ld_rec> endif


	(THE PROFILE-ANGLE RAMP, CLIMBED. Back to front the pass arrives at)
	(z_start along the cut and then runs back UP the very line the forward)
	(pass drives down before it - same two points, same wedge of metal, the)
	(other way round. Dropping it was what left the tooth standing at the)
	(top of every level on a taper: 0.4255 mm on testing_15_5, once per)
	(level, against a 0.5080 depth of cut.)
	o<pa_out> if [[#<pa_on>] AND [#<_pl_cut_rev> GT 0]]
		F#<pass_feed>
		G1 X[#<level> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<z_start>
		G1 X[#<ap_x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<ap_z>
	o<pa_out> endif

	(leave along the exit lead: blend off the pass's own direction, then the)
	(straight out to the far point. Front to back that is the lo lead at the)
	(z_end end; back to front it is the li lead at the z_start end, the same)
	(line the forward pass drives in along, travelled outward.)
	o<lead_rt> if [[#<rt_ll> GT 0] OR [#<rt_rr> GT 0]]
		#<phys_x> = #<rt_bx>
		#<end_z>  = #<rt_bz>
		(the blend radius still leaves the part, so it stays at the pass feed;)
		(only the straight retreat below runs at the lead feed. Both)
		(branches emit exactly one F, so with no lead feed set this is the)
		(same line the pass always emitted)
		o<lo_fsw> if [#<rt_ff> NE #<pass_feed>]
			F#<pass_feed>
		o<lo_fsw> else
			F#<rt_ff>
		o<lo_fsw> endif

		#<_flt_ok> = 0
		o<lo_geom> if [#<rt_rr> GT 0]
			(arrival direction at the pass end is the same pure Z travel -)
			(the lead direction is negated because fillet_lead's T1 formula)
			(assumes travel INTO T1 along -lead; a retreat actually travels)
			(OUT of T1 along +lead, so the sense fed in must be reversed to)
			(place T1 where it is actually tangent to the real straight line.)
			(rt_fz/rt_fx carries that negation already, per END, so the two)
			(directions blend on ONE circle - the entry above hands the same)
			(vector to the same utility for the same end.)
			o<fillet_lead> CALL [#<end_z>] [#<phys_x>] [-#<z_dir>] [0] [#<rt_fz>] [#<rt_fx>] [#<rt_rr>] [#<z_dir>]
		o<lo_geom> endif

		o<lo_arc> if [#<_flt_ok>]
			(traversed V-to-T1, the reverse of how the utility defines the)
			(sweep, so the direction is flipped - verified numerically by)
			(checking actual tangent direction continuity at both ends, not)
			(just that the arc is a valid circle)
			o<lo_arc_d> if [#<_flt_cw>]
				G3 X[#<_flt_t1x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<_flt_t1z> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<phys_x>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<end_z>]
			o<lo_arc_d> else
				G2 X[#<_flt_t1x> * #<_diameter_mode>] Z#<_flt_t1z> I[#<_flt_cx> - #<phys_x>] K[#<_flt_cz> - #<end_z>]
			o<lo_arc_d> endif
			#<phys_x> = #<_flt_t1x>
			#<end_z>  = #<_flt_t1z>
		o<lo_arc> endif
		o<lo_str> if [#<rt_ll> GT 0]
			o<lo_fsw2> if [#<rt_ff> NE #<pass_feed>]
				F#<rt_ff>
			o<lo_fsw2> endif
			G1 X[[#<phys_x> + #<rt_ll> * #<rt_vx>] * #<_diameter_mode>] Z[#<end_z> + #<rt_ll> * #<rt_vz>]
		o<lo_str> endif
		F#<pass_feed>
	o<lead_rt> endif

	(=== BOTH DIRECTIONS: FLIP FOR THE NEXT PASS ==========================)
	(param_dir 2 is direction 0's decomposition emitted alternately, so the)
	(next pass has to arrive at the end this one left. The flip sits HERE,)
	(past every motion, for two reasons. It is the only point that knows a)
	(pass really cut: the three returns above - blocked before the window,)
	(blocked by the multi-crossing scan, and shorter than _pl_min_pass - all)
	(leave without emitting anything, and flipping on one of those would put)
	(two consecutive cuts the same way round for a pass nobody can see. And)
	(the whole of this subroutine reads _pl_cut_rev as one value: moving the)
	(flip earlier would emit an entry lead for one direction and a retreat)
	(for the other.)
	(_pl_cut_alt is 0 for front to back and for back to front, which is why)
	(neither changes by a byte. poly_lathe_mill puts it back to 0 before the)
	(contour passes.)
	o<alt_fl> if [#<_pl_cut_alt> GT 0]
		#<_pl_cut_rev> = [1 - #<_pl_cut_rev>]
	o<alt_fl> endif

o<lathe_level_pass> endsub
